WEBVTT

00:00:01.901 --> 00:00:05.462
Captain's Log, Stardate 50203.1.

00:00:05.505 --> 00:00:08.167
We're three days away
from Enara Prime...

00:00:08.208 --> 00:00:09.334
home of the passengers

00:00:09.376 --> 00:00:12.072
we picked up from a colony
in the Fima system.

00:00:12.112 --> 00:00:15.081
Our high warp capability
has greatly reduced the time

00:00:15.115 --> 00:00:17.777
it normally takes them
to make the journey home.

00:00:17.817 --> 00:00:19.751
In return,
the Enarans have shared

00:00:19.786 --> 00:00:22.482
their energy conservation
technology with us

00:00:22.522 --> 00:00:25.650
and perhaps more importantly,
their friendship.

00:00:25.692 --> 00:00:27.216
You've never been there?

00:00:27.260 --> 00:00:29.990
Well, the trip back to the
homeland usually takes so long.

00:00:30.096 --> 00:00:31.927
I didn't want
to see it that badly.

00:00:31.965 --> 00:00:34.399
I've spent my whole life
in the Fima colony

00:00:34.434 --> 00:00:36.368
and I've always
considered it my home.

00:00:36.403 --> 00:00:37.631
You'll change your mind

00:00:37.670 --> 00:00:40.434
when you see the Daeleus
cliffs at dawn.

00:00:40.473 --> 00:00:42.873
Yes, I've heard
they're beautiful.

00:00:45.445 --> 00:00:47.913
You'll know what
"beautiful" truly means,

00:00:47.947 --> 00:00:52.384
when you stand on the
cliffs on a rainy morning

00:00:52.419 --> 00:00:55.115
and watch the raindrops...

00:00:55.155 --> 00:00:58.886
turn to mist when they
hit the molten sea.

00:00:58.925 --> 00:01:00.654
That sounds wonderful.

00:01:01.895 --> 00:01:04.193
It looks like our new components
are still slightly out of sync

00:01:04.230 --> 00:01:06.061
with your EPS system.

00:01:06.099 --> 00:01:07.225
I can't isolate it.

00:01:07.267 --> 00:01:08.791
We'll have to check
through all of them.

00:01:11.037 --> 00:01:13.130
Maybe Harry could
give us a hand.

00:01:14.507 --> 00:01:18.136
Well, I'm sure he would
if you asked him.

00:01:18.178 --> 00:01:20.373
Harry, you got a minute?

00:01:20.413 --> 00:01:21.880
Sure.

00:01:21.915 --> 00:01:24.713
Could you help us
check the modified power relays?

00:01:24.751 --> 00:01:26.275
There is a minor flow problem.

00:01:26.319 --> 00:01:28.651
I'd be happy to help.

00:01:28.688 --> 00:01:31.088
Good. Then we'll get started
first thing in the morning.

00:01:31.124 --> 00:01:33.115
Well, if we're done
for the night,

00:01:33.159 --> 00:01:35.855
maybe we could all go
get something to eat.

00:01:35.895 --> 00:01:37.692
Thank you, but I'll be
headed back to bed.

00:01:37.730 --> 00:01:41.996
I'm sure you young people
will manage without me.

00:01:42.068 --> 00:01:44.764
- Good night.
- Good night.

00:01:46.840 --> 00:01:51.504
So, I guess it'll just
be the three of us.

00:01:51.544 --> 00:01:56.004
Actually, getting some rest
sounded like a pretty good idea.

00:01:56.049 --> 00:01:58.517
Why don't you...
go on without me?

00:02:02.222 --> 00:02:04.713
No, really, I insist.

00:02:25.011 --> 00:02:26.979
What took you so long?

00:02:40.627 --> 00:02:41.753
Aah!

00:02:44.597 --> 00:02:45.564
Korenna...

00:02:45.598 --> 00:02:46.690
Shh!

00:03:02.148 --> 00:03:03.137
B'Elanna.

00:03:07.020 --> 00:03:08.487
B'Elanna, wake up.

00:03:12.091 --> 00:03:13.752
What?

00:03:13.793 --> 00:03:16.091
Your duty shift
started 20 minutes ago.

00:03:16.129 --> 00:03:17.187
I tried to reach you on the com,

00:03:17.230 --> 00:03:18.595
but you didn't answer.

00:03:21.467 --> 00:03:22.456
I guess...

00:03:22.502 --> 00:03:25.232
I guess I must have
slept right through it.

00:03:25.271 --> 00:03:26.670
Sorry.

00:03:29.609 --> 00:03:31.304
Are you feeling all right?

00:03:31.344 --> 00:03:32.311
Yes, of course.

00:03:32.345 --> 00:03:34.006
I'll be there in a minute.

00:05:24.256 --> 00:05:25.951
This is the second morning
you've been late.

00:05:26.025 --> 00:05:26.957
I'll make up the time.

00:05:27.026 --> 00:05:27.958
It won't happen again.

00:05:28.027 --> 00:05:29.585
I'm not concerned
about the duty schedule,

00:05:29.628 --> 00:05:31.095
B'Elanna.
If there's something wrong...

00:05:31.130 --> 00:05:32.256
I'm fine.

00:05:32.298 --> 00:05:34.425
You mean, fine like when
you insisted on finishing

00:05:34.466 --> 00:05:36.661
the hoverball championship
with a broken ankle?

00:05:36.702 --> 00:05:37.964
I mean there's nothing wrong.

00:05:38.070 --> 00:05:39.697
I was only late because...

00:05:39.738 --> 00:05:41.205
I've been having these dreams.

00:05:41.240 --> 00:05:42.298
They're very intense.

00:05:42.341 --> 00:05:43.330
That's all.

00:05:49.415 --> 00:05:50.973
Intensely bad?

00:05:51.050 --> 00:05:52.608
No.

00:05:52.651 --> 00:05:54.118
Just the opposite.

00:05:54.153 --> 00:05:55.950
So they're enjoyable?

00:05:55.988 --> 00:05:57.512
Stimulating?

00:05:57.556 --> 00:06:02.186
They are the most sensual dreams
I've ever had in my life...

00:06:02.227 --> 00:06:05.060
and they feel absolutely real.

00:06:08.934 --> 00:06:10.299
I don't suppose
you've been dreaming

00:06:10.336 --> 00:06:11.394
about anyone in particular?

00:06:11.437 --> 00:06:12.768
Nobody you know.

00:06:12.805 --> 00:06:14.670
Actually...

00:06:14.707 --> 00:06:16.572
he's nobody I know either.

00:06:16.609 --> 00:06:17.906
He's Enaran.

00:06:17.943 --> 00:06:19.501
One of our passengers?

00:06:19.545 --> 00:06:20.603
No. No.

00:06:20.646 --> 00:06:23.809
In the dreams, I know him.

00:06:23.849 --> 00:06:26.875
More than that,
I'm in love with him.

00:06:26.919 --> 00:06:29.080
But it's not really me
in the dream.

00:06:29.121 --> 00:06:30.884
It's somebody else entirely.

00:06:30.923 --> 00:06:33.653
In a way, it's...

00:06:33.692 --> 00:06:35.489
liberating.

00:06:35.527 --> 00:06:37.722
I'm sure.

00:06:37.763 --> 00:06:39.697
So I assume I won't
have to write up

00:06:39.732 --> 00:06:41.825
a report on your
chronic oversleeping?

00:06:41.867 --> 00:06:44.301
If you say a word
about this to anyone...

00:06:44.336 --> 00:06:47.772
I know. You'll rip my heart out
and eat it raw.

00:06:47.806 --> 00:06:50.536
Your secret's safe with me.

00:07:00.019 --> 00:07:02.351
So, what exactly
is this big surprise?

00:07:02.388 --> 00:07:03.446
All I know is that Neelix

00:07:03.489 --> 00:07:05.047
has been working
on it all afternoon.

00:07:05.090 --> 00:07:07.024
He wouldn't even let me
in there to get a snack.

00:07:16.568 --> 00:07:18.365
Welcome to Enara!

00:07:18.404 --> 00:07:20.929
It's... very...

00:07:20.973 --> 00:07:22.167
colorful.

00:07:22.207 --> 00:07:24.732
Specifically, the colors
of the Enaran flag.

00:07:24.777 --> 00:07:26.836
The decor, the music, the menu...

00:07:26.879 --> 00:07:28.904
all authentically Enaran.

00:07:28.947 --> 00:07:31.108
What happened
to the tables and chairs?

00:07:31.150 --> 00:07:33.243
Enarans don't use them.

00:07:33.285 --> 00:07:36.846
After a big meal, you can
just lie back and take a nap.

00:07:36.889 --> 00:07:38.117
Very practical.

00:07:38.157 --> 00:07:40.352
It's a little cold in here,
isn't it?

00:07:40.392 --> 00:07:42.553
Perhaps a bit chillier
than we're used to,

00:07:42.594 --> 00:07:44.494
but just about perfect for...

00:07:44.530 --> 00:07:46.896
Enarans. I got it.

00:07:46.932 --> 00:07:50.527
You must try some of these
delightful algae puffs.

00:07:50.569 --> 00:07:51.968
They're fresh from the oven.

00:07:52.004 --> 00:07:53.232
Harry?

00:07:55.441 --> 00:07:57.033
Maybe later.

00:08:33.846 --> 00:08:35.541
Oh, that was wonderful.

00:08:35.581 --> 00:08:37.378
What a lovely piece of music.

00:08:37.416 --> 00:08:39.748
You should thank Jora Mirell.

00:08:39.785 --> 00:08:41.377
She composed it.

00:08:41.420 --> 00:08:45.686
I still think you're
rushing the harmonics

00:08:45.724 --> 00:08:47.885
in the second movement.

00:08:47.926 --> 00:08:49.450
I love music.

00:08:49.495 --> 00:08:50.462
I've always regretted

00:08:50.496 --> 00:08:52.487
that I never learned
to play an instrument.

00:08:52.531 --> 00:08:55.261
I'd be glad
to help you if you like.

00:08:55.300 --> 00:08:57.768
I'd like it very much.

00:08:57.803 --> 00:09:00.431
I'm sure I could find time
for a few lessons.

00:09:27.966 --> 00:09:29.058
Captain?

00:09:29.101 --> 00:09:30.796
I'm all right.

00:09:30.836 --> 00:09:33.270
I did understand you correctly

00:09:33.305 --> 00:09:35.466
that you wanted to share
my knowledge of music?

00:09:36.875 --> 00:09:38.570
I didn't realize
you were offering

00:09:38.610 --> 00:09:39.872
to share it so directly.

00:09:39.912 --> 00:09:41.641
The sensation
was just a little...

00:09:41.680 --> 00:09:42.840
overwhelming.

00:09:42.881 --> 00:09:45.179
I am terribly sorry, Captain.

00:09:45.217 --> 00:09:48.550
I assumed since you knew
of our telepathic abilities...

00:09:48.587 --> 00:09:51.852
I-I never would have dreamed
of making a connection

00:09:51.890 --> 00:09:53.255
without your consent.

00:09:53.292 --> 00:09:55.157
You intended
to give me a gift...

00:09:56.628 --> 00:09:57.959
and it was wonderful.

00:09:58.063 --> 00:10:00.497
Your abilities
allow you to transfer

00:10:00.532 --> 00:10:03.399
knowledge from your
own mind to another's?

00:10:03.435 --> 00:10:05.562
Not precisely.

00:10:05.604 --> 00:10:07.868
We're able to share
our experiences

00:10:07.906 --> 00:10:09.635
through a telepathic link.

00:10:09.675 --> 00:10:12.906
I remembered lessons
and hours of practice.

00:10:12.945 --> 00:10:15.539
Were those your experiences?

00:10:15.581 --> 00:10:17.310
Intriguing.

00:10:19.117 --> 00:10:20.675
Remarkable.

00:10:25.757 --> 00:10:28.726
You take a couple of these...

00:10:28.760 --> 00:10:30.990
roll them around like this...

00:10:31.096 --> 00:10:33.428
and voila!

00:10:33.465 --> 00:10:36.457
Your hands are clean
and disinfected.

00:10:36.501 --> 00:10:38.992
The Enarans are very hygienic.

00:10:39.037 --> 00:10:40.698
Hmm.

00:10:40.739 --> 00:10:43.708
I haven't seen Lieutenant Torres
around here tonight.

00:10:43.742 --> 00:10:44.970
I suppose she's putting in

00:10:45.010 --> 00:10:46.705
another late night
in Engineering.

00:10:46.745 --> 00:10:47.712
Actually, I think

00:10:47.746 --> 00:10:49.680
she might have gone
to bed early tonight.

00:11:03.996 --> 00:11:06.362
I'm not one to dictate
who your friends are,

00:11:06.398 --> 00:11:08.525
but I'm sure you can see
as clearly as I can

00:11:08.567 --> 00:11:11.468
that some friends
are less suitable than others.

00:11:11.503 --> 00:11:13.869
Like Dathan?

00:11:13.906 --> 00:11:16.807
Yes. You promised
you wouldn't see him anymore

00:11:16.842 --> 00:11:17.968
and then I heard
you were talking

00:11:18.010 --> 00:11:19.739
to him again the other day.

00:11:19.778 --> 00:11:21.609
He came up to me on the street.

00:11:21.647 --> 00:11:23.239
I couldn't help it.

00:11:23.282 --> 00:11:26.649
Korenna, don't you see

00:11:26.685 --> 00:11:28.619
I am thinking of him
as well as you?

00:11:28.654 --> 00:11:30.781
Now, you only
encourage him this way

00:11:30.822 --> 00:11:32.414
and that isn't very fair, is it?

00:11:32.457 --> 00:11:34.482
What isn't fair is
that you treat him

00:11:34.526 --> 00:11:35.493
like everybody else.

00:11:35.527 --> 00:11:36.687
He's different.

00:11:36.728 --> 00:11:39.458
If you just talked to him,
you'd understand that.

00:11:39.498 --> 00:11:41.932
You know, one of the things
I love about you most

00:11:41.967 --> 00:11:43.958
is your compassion for others.

00:11:44.002 --> 00:11:45.435
But you're still young.

00:11:45.470 --> 00:11:47.370
You don't realize that
there are some people

00:11:47.406 --> 00:11:49.636
that might take advantage
of that compassion.

00:11:49.675 --> 00:11:52.007
Now, I want you to promise me,

00:11:52.077 --> 00:11:54.511
if he comes up to you again,
you'll just walk away.

00:11:54.546 --> 00:11:56.537
That should be clear enough.

00:11:56.581 --> 00:11:58.742
I'm sure.

00:12:00.285 --> 00:12:02.651
And finish your tarin juice.

00:12:02.688 --> 00:12:04.349
It's good for you.

00:12:23.575 --> 00:12:25.270
He's gone.

00:12:28.814 --> 00:12:29.974
I should go.

00:12:30.048 --> 00:12:31.675
He's leaving for work soon.

00:12:31.717 --> 00:12:33.446
It's safer to wait.

00:12:36.154 --> 00:12:39.612
You know,
this will only encourage me.

00:12:39.658 --> 00:12:42.559
I hope so.

00:13:05.183 --> 00:13:06.980
No! No!

00:13:15.961 --> 00:13:17.758
We've completed
the modifications

00:13:17.796 --> 00:13:19.354
on the primary EPS conduits.

00:13:19.398 --> 00:13:21.457
I have a crew starting
on the backup systems.

00:13:21.500 --> 00:13:24.230
Can you get it done
before we drop off the Enarans?

00:13:24.269 --> 00:13:27.329
Yes. We'll have to pull
some longer shifts,

00:13:27.372 --> 00:13:30.170
but two more days should do it.

00:13:33.578 --> 00:13:35.273
Is there something
else on your mind?

00:13:37.249 --> 00:13:39.149
Those dreams I've been having...

00:13:41.486 --> 00:13:43.818
um, they're getting
kind of strange.

00:13:43.855 --> 00:13:45.948
In what way?

00:13:45.991 --> 00:13:51.224
Last night,
in the middle of the dream,

00:13:51.263 --> 00:13:53.356
I was...

00:13:53.398 --> 00:13:59.166
kissing him... my lover...
and suddenly he was dead.

00:13:59.204 --> 00:14:00.694
Burned.

00:14:00.739 --> 00:14:02.707
B'Elanna...

00:14:02.741 --> 00:14:05.539
But there's more going on
than just a love affair.

00:14:05.577 --> 00:14:08.137
I'm having a relationship
with this man,

00:14:08.180 --> 00:14:11.877
but my father doesn't approve,
so we have to sneak around.

00:14:11.917 --> 00:14:16.820
It's like each new dream
advances the story.

00:14:16.855 --> 00:14:18.220
It sounds like a holonovel.

00:14:18.256 --> 00:14:20.520
But it feels like
it's actually happening.

00:14:20.559 --> 00:14:22.754
I mean, physically, emotionally,

00:14:22.794 --> 00:14:24.921
it's no different
from real life.

00:14:24.963 --> 00:14:28.228
I've never had dreams
like this before.

00:14:28.266 --> 00:14:30.131
It can't be a coincidence
that this is going on

00:14:30.168 --> 00:14:31.965
while we have a group
of telepaths on board.

00:14:32.003 --> 00:14:33.732
Exactly.

00:14:33.772 --> 00:14:36.707
I want to find out more
about what these Enarans can do.

00:14:36.741 --> 00:14:39.301
Why don't you ask your
friend in Engineering?

00:14:39.344 --> 00:14:40.538
I'm going to.

00:14:40.579 --> 00:14:41.876
I'll talk to the Captain.

00:14:41.913 --> 00:14:45.144
She should know about anything
that might involve our guests.

00:14:45.183 --> 00:14:46.207
Right.

00:14:54.092 --> 00:14:56.390
Once, I stood where you are

00:14:56.428 --> 00:14:59.989
during the early days
of interstellar exploration.

00:15:00.065 --> 00:15:03.125
It was an important
leap forward for our people

00:15:03.168 --> 00:15:05.295
and I was proud
to be part of it.

00:15:05.337 --> 00:15:08.898
Today, with the advent
of terraforming, we stand ready

00:15:08.940 --> 00:15:12.137
to take another leap forward
into an era

00:15:12.177 --> 00:15:15.169
of expansion and colonization.

00:15:15.213 --> 00:15:18.307
You will show us the way.

00:15:18.350 --> 00:15:20.841
There are some
who resist progress.

00:15:20.886 --> 00:15:24.947
Do not let the voices
of fear and ignorance

00:15:24.990 --> 00:15:26.617
discourage you.

00:15:26.658 --> 00:15:30.754
Claim your rightful place
as leaders of a new era.

00:15:30.795 --> 00:15:34.322
The future of Enara
is in your hands.

00:15:37.502 --> 00:15:41.404
Now, today, we honor
a group of young people

00:15:41.439 --> 00:15:44.306
who represent our best hope
for that future.

00:15:44.342 --> 00:15:45.604
It is a great pleasure to give

00:15:45.644 --> 00:15:48.511
this first award
to my own daughter, Korenna.

00:15:57.155 --> 00:15:59.180
I'm so very proud of you.

00:16:19.844 --> 00:16:21.641
It looks good on you.

00:16:25.716 --> 00:16:28.378
What are you doing here?

00:16:29.654 --> 00:16:31.281
Today's important for you.

00:16:31.322 --> 00:16:32.448
I wanted to be here.

00:16:32.490 --> 00:16:35.186
I'm glad you came.

00:16:38.162 --> 00:16:40.130
I know this award
will help me get

00:16:40.164 --> 00:16:42.189
into the District
Education Center.

00:16:42.233 --> 00:16:45.031
I could be a junior instructor
in less than a year.

00:16:46.737 --> 00:16:48.432
I'm really happy for you.

00:16:48.472 --> 00:16:50.531
Maybe you could take
the entrance examination, too.

00:16:50.574 --> 00:16:51.973
You know that's impossible.

00:16:52.009 --> 00:16:53.340
I can't go to the Center.

00:16:53.377 --> 00:16:56.437
Nothing is impossible
if you want it badly enough.

00:16:58.449 --> 00:17:00.314
I want us to be together.

00:17:00.351 --> 00:17:02.546
I love you, Korenna.

00:17:05.222 --> 00:17:07.656
It's just so frustrating.

00:17:07.692 --> 00:17:10.525
I can't stand being away
from you all the time.

00:17:10.561 --> 00:17:11.528
Oh, I know.

00:17:11.562 --> 00:17:15.259
Oh, I wish I could hold you
right now.

00:17:20.271 --> 00:17:22.899
What would you do if you could?

00:17:26.210 --> 00:17:27.370
I'll show you.

00:17:36.520 --> 00:17:37.487
I'll see you tonight.

00:17:37.521 --> 00:17:39.614
No! No! There's going
to be a big dinner

00:17:39.657 --> 00:17:41.022
with my father's friends.

00:17:42.593 --> 00:17:44.151
Tomorrow night, then.

00:17:44.195 --> 00:17:46.186
Tomorrow.

00:17:47.365 --> 00:17:48.457
Single file.

00:17:48.499 --> 00:17:49.659
Identification.

00:17:50.468 --> 00:17:53.301
Next.

00:17:53.337 --> 00:17:54.895
Let's go.

00:17:54.939 --> 00:17:56.634
Have identification ready.

00:17:56.674 --> 00:17:57.971
This way, this way.

00:17:58.876 --> 00:18:00.571
All the way out.

00:18:03.447 --> 00:18:05.005
Let's move.

00:18:08.419 --> 00:18:09.909
B'Elanna!

00:18:09.954 --> 00:18:12.149
Can you hear me?

00:18:12.189 --> 00:18:14.987
Kes to Sick Bay.
Medical emergency.

00:18:26.670 --> 00:18:28.570
Good to see you're awake,
Lieutenant.

00:18:30.274 --> 00:18:31.741
What happened?

00:18:31.776 --> 00:18:32.743
I found you unconscious

00:18:32.777 --> 00:18:35.211
in the corridor
near Engineering.

00:18:38.049 --> 00:18:40.210
I was dreaming again.

00:18:40.251 --> 00:18:43.379
Not according to your
cortical theta wave readings.

00:18:43.421 --> 00:18:44.786
The pattern clearly indicated

00:18:44.822 --> 00:18:46.551
that you were
experiencing memories.

00:18:46.590 --> 00:18:48.820
Specifically,
implanted memories.

00:18:48.859 --> 00:18:50.190
Implanted?

00:18:50.227 --> 00:18:51.854
By the Enarans?

00:18:51.896 --> 00:18:54.387
There's strong evidence
of telepathic activity

00:18:54.432 --> 00:18:55.660
in your frontal lobe.

00:18:55.699 --> 00:18:58.065
My experience with
the Enarans' telepathy

00:18:58.102 --> 00:19:00.002
seems to be very different
from yours.

00:19:01.405 --> 00:19:03.498
Jor Brel was standing near me

00:19:03.541 --> 00:19:05.771
when I received his memories.

00:19:05.810 --> 00:19:08.244
Were there any Enarans near
you when you had your dreams?

00:19:08.279 --> 00:19:10.372
No, I was alone every time.

00:19:10.414 --> 00:19:14.180
You've also been asleep
or unconscious every time.

00:19:14.218 --> 00:19:16.413
The shared memories feel like...

00:19:16.454 --> 00:19:19.184
vivid dreams to you.

00:19:19.223 --> 00:19:20.554
In the Lieutenant's case,
the memories

00:19:20.591 --> 00:19:22.752
seem to have been placed
in her unconscious.

00:19:22.793 --> 00:19:24.283
They're only emerging
when her conscious mind

00:19:24.328 --> 00:19:25.659
is inactive.

00:19:25.696 --> 00:19:27.186
Why did she pass out?

00:19:27.231 --> 00:19:29.563
The synaptic patterns
of the implanted memories

00:19:29.600 --> 00:19:32.592
are not quite compatible
with her neural pathways.

00:19:32.636 --> 00:19:34.797
There's been some minor cortical
damage, which I've corrected.

00:19:34.839 --> 00:19:36.807
Can you prevent further damage?

00:19:36.841 --> 00:19:39.935
This inhibitor will control
her theta wave activity.

00:19:39.977 --> 00:19:42.571
That should suppress
the memories.

00:19:42.613 --> 00:19:44.046
I won't have any more
of the dreams?

00:19:44.081 --> 00:19:45.708
That's the idea.

00:19:47.151 --> 00:19:48.118
What's wrong?

00:19:49.153 --> 00:19:51.280
If the dreams stop,

00:19:51.322 --> 00:19:53.688
I'll never know what happens
to these people.

00:19:53.724 --> 00:19:59.253
I mean, this woman, Korenna,
I... I feel what she feels.

00:19:59.296 --> 00:20:02.356
And right now, she is
torn and confused

00:20:02.399 --> 00:20:03.627
about her loyalties,

00:20:03.667 --> 00:20:06.067
and I don't know what I'm...
what she's going to do.

00:20:06.103 --> 00:20:08.230
I don't think satisfying
your curiosity

00:20:08.272 --> 00:20:10.672
is worth risking brain damage,
Lieutenant.

00:20:15.746 --> 00:20:18.374
I'm giving you the next
two days off duty.

00:20:18.415 --> 00:20:20.383
Use them to rest.

00:20:20.417 --> 00:20:21.975
I'll speak with Brel,

00:20:22.019 --> 00:20:23.509
and find out
what's happening to you.

00:20:23.554 --> 00:20:25.419
I'd like to come with you,
Captain.

00:20:25.456 --> 00:20:27.481
I'd rest a lot better
if I had some answers.

00:20:29.994 --> 00:20:31.086
I find it impossible

00:20:31.128 --> 00:20:33.528
that any of us could be
doing this purposely.

00:20:33.564 --> 00:20:35.088
You do possess the capability

00:20:35.132 --> 00:20:37.566
to share your experiences
without mutual consent.

00:20:37.601 --> 00:20:40.764
Yes, but, uh,
it just isn't done.

00:20:40.804 --> 00:20:42.169
I-I know that we had

00:20:42.206 --> 00:20:44.606
a misunderstanding before,
Captain,

00:20:44.642 --> 00:20:47.270
but I assure you,
we have strict ethics.

00:20:47.311 --> 00:20:49.108
We're not suggesting otherwise.

00:20:49.146 --> 00:20:51.614
We're only trying to find out
how this is happening.

00:20:51.649 --> 00:20:53.549
Well, I have heard of instances

00:20:53.584 --> 00:20:57.145
where members of some alien
races have been affected

00:20:57.188 --> 00:20:59.986
by the slight telepathic field
we generate, but nothing

00:21:00.024 --> 00:21:02.857
as intense as what
your Lieutenant has described.

00:21:02.893 --> 00:21:06.329
Well, according to our Doctor,
they're memories.

00:21:06.363 --> 00:21:07.796
That's possible.

00:21:07.831 --> 00:21:10.356
She may be picking up
stray thoughts and memories

00:21:10.401 --> 00:21:13.564
from every Enaran on the ship.

00:21:13.604 --> 00:21:16.630
It must be terribly confusing.

00:21:16.674 --> 00:21:18.403
Perhaps that's why her
mind has organized it

00:21:18.442 --> 00:21:20.342
into a kind of narrative.

00:21:20.377 --> 00:21:22.845
Are you saying that
I'm making this all up?

00:21:22.880 --> 00:21:23.869
No, no, no.

00:21:23.914 --> 00:21:25.814
Some elements
may very well have come

00:21:25.849 --> 00:21:27.407
from our actual experiences.

00:21:27.451 --> 00:21:29.851
I confess I...
I may have crawled

00:21:29.887 --> 00:21:32.082
into a bedroom window or two
in my youth.

00:21:32.122 --> 00:21:35.614
You mentioned
a citizenship award.

00:21:35.659 --> 00:21:39.527
There are several past
recipients in our group.

00:21:39.563 --> 00:21:43.761
We may be each contributing some
small details to your story.

00:21:43.801 --> 00:21:46.998
Nothing really happened
the way I remember it?

00:21:47.104 --> 00:21:49.334
It's highly unlikely.

00:21:53.444 --> 00:21:56.208
We appreciate your help,
Jor Brel.

00:21:57.681 --> 00:22:00.343
I wish there was something more
that I could do.

00:22:00.384 --> 00:22:03.376
I truly regret any ill effects

00:22:03.420 --> 00:22:05.513
that our presence here
has caused you.

00:22:05.556 --> 00:22:08.389
Well, fortunately, those
effects are under control now.

00:22:08.425 --> 00:22:10.950
The Doctor was able
to suppress the memories.

00:22:10.995 --> 00:22:13.225
I'm very glad to hear that.

00:22:17.401 --> 00:22:20.199
His explanation is plausible.

00:22:20.237 --> 00:22:21.602
B'Elanna?

00:22:21.639 --> 00:22:24.233
I don't know.

00:22:24.275 --> 00:22:27.073
Those dreams are so real...

00:22:27.111 --> 00:22:28.976
Maybe he's right.

00:22:29.013 --> 00:22:30.378
The Enarans haven't

00:22:30.414 --> 00:22:32.746
shown any hint of subterfuge...
any hidden agenda.

00:22:32.783 --> 00:22:35.308
They've been nothing
but straightforward and honest.

00:22:35.352 --> 00:22:37.286
You're in no immediate danger.

00:22:37.321 --> 00:22:38.879
They'll be gone in another day.

00:22:38.922 --> 00:22:40.890
The situation
will resolve itself.

00:22:40.924 --> 00:22:44.587
And yet, you fully intend
to continue investigating.

00:22:44.628 --> 00:22:46.152
I wonder how long it's been

00:22:46.196 --> 00:22:48.494
since I did anything
that surprised you.

00:22:49.933 --> 00:22:51.958
I share your concern, Captain.

00:22:52.002 --> 00:22:53.936
We haven't ruled out
the possibility

00:22:53.971 --> 00:22:55.836
that this may be
a deliberate act.

00:22:57.107 --> 00:22:58.665
I want to talk to more
of the Enarans,

00:22:58.709 --> 00:22:59.903
see what they have to say.

00:22:59.943 --> 00:23:01.467
I'll talk to Jessen and Mirell.

00:23:01.512 --> 00:23:03.139
They've been working with me
in Engineering.

00:23:03.180 --> 00:23:04.442
You've done enough already,
B'Elanna.

00:23:04.481 --> 00:23:05.812
I want you to get some rest.

00:23:05.849 --> 00:23:06.941
But...

00:23:07.017 --> 00:23:08.075
You need to get away from this.

00:23:08.118 --> 00:23:09.107
We'll take it from here.

00:23:11.622 --> 00:23:15.615
Captain's Log, Stardate 50211.4.

00:23:15.659 --> 00:23:17.183
We're approaching Enara

00:23:17.227 --> 00:23:20.492
and preparing to host
a farewell party for our guests.

00:23:20.531 --> 00:23:22.362
They've made every effort
to help us understand

00:23:22.399 --> 00:23:25.095
their telepathic abilities,
but it's still a mystery

00:23:25.135 --> 00:23:28.593
why they've affected
Lieutenant Torres so strongly.

00:24:10.614 --> 00:24:11.979
Korenna, are you ready?

00:24:15.419 --> 00:24:17.216
You'll do well.

00:24:17.254 --> 00:24:19.017
I'll be there with you.

00:24:20.724 --> 00:24:23.249
This is all voluntary, isn't it?

00:24:23.293 --> 00:24:24.521
They want to be resettled?

00:24:24.561 --> 00:24:25.721
Of course.

00:24:27.197 --> 00:24:28.926
Although, it's impossible
to understand

00:24:28.966 --> 00:24:31.400
what these Regressives want.

00:24:31.435 --> 00:24:33.494
They simply don't think
like we do.

00:24:34.538 --> 00:24:36.870
How do we relate to people

00:24:36.907 --> 00:24:41.276
who refuse all but the most
primitive technology?

00:24:41.311 --> 00:24:44.747
Who live their lives without
a communications interlink

00:24:44.782 --> 00:24:46.977
or microfusion generators?

00:24:47.084 --> 00:24:49.177
If that's the way
they want to live...

00:24:49.219 --> 00:24:51.084
why can't they?

00:24:51.121 --> 00:24:52.088
Well, they can.

00:24:52.122 --> 00:24:53.953
That's why we're
helping them to resettle,

00:24:53.991 --> 00:24:55.982
so that they can be
completely comfortable

00:24:56.093 --> 00:24:58.357
practicing a way of life
that they've chosen.

00:24:58.395 --> 00:25:00.363
They could do that here

00:25:00.397 --> 00:25:02.524
in their village.

00:25:02.566 --> 00:25:03.726
Well, you wouldn't say that

00:25:03.767 --> 00:25:05.029
if you'd ever been
inside that place.

00:25:06.570 --> 00:25:09.471
Do you realize they won't
even use radioseptics

00:25:09.506 --> 00:25:12.805
to sterilize their homes,
or their hands before they eat?

00:25:12.843 --> 00:25:16.609
It's a miracle they haven't
started a plague by now.

00:25:16.647 --> 00:25:21.949
Then... it's dangerous
to have them living here.

00:25:21.985 --> 00:25:23.384
Yes, it is.

00:25:23.420 --> 00:25:26.548
And we've been tolerant
for a very long time,

00:25:26.590 --> 00:25:29.252
but I think by now
even they realize

00:25:29.293 --> 00:25:31.887
that they'd be better off
living somewhere else.

00:25:31.929 --> 00:25:33.726
But some of them
want to stay here.

00:25:33.764 --> 00:25:37.222
Well, there are always some
people who resist change

00:25:37.267 --> 00:25:39.258
even if they know
it's best for them,

00:25:39.303 --> 00:25:42.932
but once they see
their friends and family

00:25:42.973 --> 00:25:44.634
happily settled
in the new colony,

00:25:44.675 --> 00:25:46.006
they'll want to go as well.

00:25:57.454 --> 00:25:58.478
Demalos.

00:25:58.522 --> 00:26:00.046
Demalos, move along.

00:26:02.526 --> 00:26:04.960
- Sanric.
- Sanric.

00:26:06.897 --> 00:26:08.387
Farran.

00:26:08.432 --> 00:26:10.491
What's going to happen to us?

00:26:10.534 --> 00:26:13.094
You'll have a new place
to live with your own kind.

00:26:13.136 --> 00:26:14.626
You'll be much happier there.

00:26:14.671 --> 00:26:15.638
Please...

00:26:15.672 --> 00:26:17.037
- Move it along.
...can you tell me...

00:26:17.074 --> 00:26:18.598
I only want to know
where we're going.

00:26:18.642 --> 00:26:19.734
Peshar.

00:26:22.713 --> 00:26:24.476
Alaris.

00:26:27.050 --> 00:26:28.347
Dathan Alaris!

00:26:34.525 --> 00:26:35.492
Where is he?

00:26:35.526 --> 00:26:36.493
He couldn't be leaving today.

00:26:36.527 --> 00:26:37.494
Did you warn him?

00:26:37.528 --> 00:26:38.961
Did you tell him
he was on the list?

00:26:39.029 --> 00:26:41.156
I didn't even know that he was.

00:26:41.198 --> 00:26:43.223
You put his name there,
didn't you?

00:26:43.267 --> 00:26:44.700
To keep him away from me.

00:26:44.735 --> 00:26:46.100
Fredik! Don't!

00:26:46.136 --> 00:26:47.125
No!

00:26:55.078 --> 00:26:57.205
Computer, locate Jora Mirell.

00:26:57.247 --> 00:26:59.374
Jora Mirell is in her quarters.

00:27:19.433 --> 00:27:20.798
I'll get you to Sick Bay.

00:27:20.834 --> 00:27:21.823
No.

00:27:22.970 --> 00:27:26.667
I have to give you
the rest of it.

00:27:30.077 --> 00:27:31.942
You are Korenna.

00:27:34.148 --> 00:27:36.173
These are your memories.

00:27:37.217 --> 00:27:38.548
Yes.

00:27:40.721 --> 00:27:42.621
Why give them to me?

00:27:42.656 --> 00:27:45.784
You won't deny the truth.

00:27:45.826 --> 00:27:49.284
We've been hiding it.

00:27:49.329 --> 00:27:52.628
I couldn't anymore.

00:27:52.666 --> 00:27:56.363
They found out
I was sharing it with you.

00:27:56.403 --> 00:27:57.961
Who did?

00:27:58.071 --> 00:28:01.404
Don't let the memories die.

00:28:01.441 --> 00:28:02.908
Promise me.

00:28:02.976 --> 00:28:04.273
I don't understand...

00:28:31.805 --> 00:28:32.863
My father's home.

00:28:32.906 --> 00:28:34.066
If he hears you...

00:28:34.107 --> 00:28:35.904
What happened?

00:28:35.943 --> 00:28:37.740
One of your friends
made some trouble

00:28:37.778 --> 00:28:39.439
on the resettlement line today.

00:28:39.479 --> 00:28:40.605
You were on the list, too.

00:28:40.647 --> 00:28:41.614
Where were you?

00:28:41.648 --> 00:28:42.808
Some of us got away.

00:28:42.850 --> 00:28:44.511
We're leaving tonight.

00:28:44.551 --> 00:28:47.520
Come with me.

00:28:47.554 --> 00:28:50.523
Korenna, it's the only way
we can be together now.

00:28:52.459 --> 00:28:54.518
You're asking me
to abandon my family,

00:28:54.561 --> 00:28:55.585
my career...

00:28:55.629 --> 00:28:57.494
Yes, I am.
Leave it all behind.

00:28:57.531 --> 00:28:59.055
What's happening here
is wrong, Korenna.

00:28:59.099 --> 00:29:00.259
Don't be a part of it anymore.

00:29:00.300 --> 00:29:01.528
It's just a resettlement.

00:29:01.568 --> 00:29:02.899
It is more than that.

00:29:02.936 --> 00:29:05.166
My uncle and his family
were resettled two months ago

00:29:05.205 --> 00:29:06.763
and we haven't heard
from them since.

00:29:06.807 --> 00:29:09.002
Nobody I know
has had any contact

00:29:09.042 --> 00:29:11.010
with this new colony
we're supposed to be going to.

00:29:11.044 --> 00:29:12.636
There could be
a perfectly good reason...

00:29:12.679 --> 00:29:14.169
There are stories.

00:29:14.214 --> 00:29:16.614
I've heard that the transports
don't really go anywhere,

00:29:16.650 --> 00:29:19.141
that the passengers
just get vaporized

00:29:19.186 --> 00:29:20.483
in some kind of thermal sweep.

00:29:20.520 --> 00:29:22.488
Korenna, thousands of us
have gone already.

00:29:22.522 --> 00:29:23.546
We are being slaughtered.

00:29:23.590 --> 00:29:24.852
It's ridiculous.

00:29:24.892 --> 00:29:26.917
No one is being killed.

00:29:26.994 --> 00:29:27.926
My father told me...

00:29:28.028 --> 00:29:29.689
Your father is lying to you!

00:29:30.697 --> 00:29:32.858
I'm sorry, but you have
got to make a choice.

00:29:32.900 --> 00:29:35.494
You can't go on trying to
believe in both of us anymore.

00:29:35.535 --> 00:29:37.833
Either he is right and you
should never see me again,

00:29:37.871 --> 00:29:41.773
or I'm right and he is part
of a terrible crime.

00:29:41.808 --> 00:29:44.368
No. My father is a good man.

00:29:44.411 --> 00:29:46.038
I can show you
how we're rounded up

00:29:46.079 --> 00:29:47.706
for these voluntary
resettlements,

00:29:47.748 --> 00:29:49.306
how the soldiers
treat Regressives

00:29:49.349 --> 00:29:50.373
who won't go quietly.

00:29:50.417 --> 00:29:52.749
I know it is hard to face,
but you have to.

00:29:52.786 --> 00:29:53.878
It is too important.

00:29:53.921 --> 00:29:54.888
- Now let me show you.
- No, I...

00:29:55.923 --> 00:29:57.857
Korenna?

00:30:05.766 --> 00:30:06.926
Come in.

00:30:10.504 --> 00:30:12.335
I was, I was just practicing.

00:30:14.541 --> 00:30:16.270
I've always said
you have the talent

00:30:16.310 --> 00:30:17.470
to play professionally.

00:30:19.646 --> 00:30:21.273
How are you feeling?

00:30:21.315 --> 00:30:23.783
I've been better.

00:30:23.817 --> 00:30:25.717
Don't think about it anymore.

00:30:25.752 --> 00:30:28.414
That Regressive was
completely irrational.

00:30:28.455 --> 00:30:30.423
He attacked you for no reason.

00:30:30.457 --> 00:30:32.254
Maybe he thought
he had a reason.

00:30:32.292 --> 00:30:33.987
Maybe he was afraid.

00:30:38.131 --> 00:30:40.565
I know there are some
very disturbing rumors

00:30:40.600 --> 00:30:42.625
coming from these people.

00:30:42.669 --> 00:30:45.536
You may have heard them
from that boy.

00:30:56.917 --> 00:30:58.976
You know, the thing
that is so insidious

00:30:59.019 --> 00:31:00.247
about these Regressives

00:31:00.287 --> 00:31:02.118
is that they pretend
to be passive,

00:31:02.155 --> 00:31:03.747
not harming anyone

00:31:03.790 --> 00:31:06.782
and all the while
they are spreading their lies,

00:31:06.827 --> 00:31:09.694
trying to make you believe
these awful things.

00:31:09.730 --> 00:31:10.890
Why would they do that?

00:31:10.931 --> 00:31:16.426
They have some twisted ideas
about resisting progress,

00:31:16.470 --> 00:31:17.937
which they think
gives them the right

00:31:17.971 --> 00:31:19.734
to hold us back
in any way that they can.

00:31:19.773 --> 00:31:24.972
They're trying to undermine us,
to cause dissent and doubt.

00:31:26.680 --> 00:31:29.308
Just look at how
they've affected you.

00:31:31.918 --> 00:31:33.818
But...

00:31:33.854 --> 00:31:36.687
what they're saying
is so horrible.

00:31:36.723 --> 00:31:39.692
Yes,
but it isn't very plausible.

00:31:39.726 --> 00:31:42.092
Korenna, think.

00:31:42.129 --> 00:31:45.189
A secret conspiracy
against their people?

00:31:45.232 --> 00:31:48.633
Organized murder
on such an enormous scale?

00:31:48.668 --> 00:31:51.603
Do you really believe
that your family and friends

00:31:51.638 --> 00:31:53.435
are capable of that?

00:31:57.044 --> 00:31:58.011
No.

00:31:58.045 --> 00:31:59.103
'Course not.

00:31:59.146 --> 00:32:01.944
Now, I know how hard it is
for you to accept

00:32:02.015 --> 00:32:04.347
that anyone, even Regressives,

00:32:04.384 --> 00:32:06.318
could lie
about something like that,

00:32:06.353 --> 00:32:08.651
but it is all part
of their manipulation.

00:32:08.688 --> 00:32:10.952
These people have no conscience.

00:32:11.058 --> 00:32:13.583
They'll say anything
to get what they want.

00:32:15.062 --> 00:32:17.155
Like that boy Dathan.

00:32:28.508 --> 00:32:31.306
Has he told you
he's in love with you?

00:32:33.680 --> 00:32:34.874
He's not.

00:32:37.317 --> 00:32:39.478
It's his way
of gaining your sympathy.

00:32:41.922 --> 00:32:44.117
And not only yours.

00:32:44.157 --> 00:32:47.786
I've seen him talking to quite
a number of young women.

00:32:52.232 --> 00:32:54.894
Has he been asking you
to trust him?

00:32:54.935 --> 00:32:58.336
He's poisoning you
against your own people.

00:32:59.706 --> 00:33:01.901
Even your own family.

00:33:01.942 --> 00:33:04.137
Hmm?

00:33:10.016 --> 00:33:11.506
That's very cruel.

00:33:13.820 --> 00:33:16.015
No wonder you've been confused.

00:33:17.691 --> 00:33:20.990
But now you understand what
these people are really like.

00:33:51.258 --> 00:33:52.225
You!

00:33:52.259 --> 00:33:53.226
No.

00:33:54.261 --> 00:33:55.250
No.

00:34:23.957 --> 00:34:25.857
These criminals represent

00:34:25.892 --> 00:34:28.053
a growing threat
to Enaran society.

00:34:28.094 --> 00:34:30.858
As responsible citizens,
we must fight back!

00:34:33.400 --> 00:34:35.698
With their punishment,

00:34:35.735 --> 00:34:38.203
we send a clear signal
to all Regressives.

00:34:38.238 --> 00:34:41.503
We will protect
ourselves and our ideals

00:34:41.541 --> 00:34:43.441
from their
destructive influence

00:34:43.476 --> 00:34:45.000
by whatever means necessary.

00:34:56.723 --> 00:35:01.683
Yes! Yes! Yes! Yes!

00:35:01.728 --> 00:35:06.358
Yes! Yes! Yes!
Yes!

00:35:09.836 --> 00:35:12.396
Why did they all move away?

00:35:12.439 --> 00:35:14.930
Because they didn't want to live
with the rest of us anymore.

00:35:15.008 --> 00:35:16.100
Why?

00:35:16.142 --> 00:35:19.339
The Regressive people
had very strange ideas

00:35:19.379 --> 00:35:20.812
about how to live.

00:35:20.847 --> 00:35:22.542
They didn't want
to learn new things

00:35:22.582 --> 00:35:24.379
or use any of the technology

00:35:24.417 --> 00:35:26.476
that we tried to share
with them.

00:35:26.519 --> 00:35:29.317
They decided to live
somewhere else on their own

00:35:29.356 --> 00:35:31.085
and we let them go.

00:35:31.124 --> 00:35:34.093
But they couldn't take
very good care of themselves.

00:35:34.127 --> 00:35:36.095
They fought with each other.

00:35:36.129 --> 00:35:39.064
They spread
all kinds of diseases.

00:35:39.099 --> 00:35:40.396
And they all died?

00:35:40.433 --> 00:35:42.731
They destroyed themselves.

00:35:42.769 --> 00:35:45.465
It was very sad.

00:35:45.505 --> 00:35:50.442
But... we can learn
from their mistakes.

00:35:50.477 --> 00:35:52.638
That's why we keep
this gate here...

00:35:52.679 --> 00:35:57.173
to remind us never to be
stubborn and backward

00:35:57.217 --> 00:35:58.241
like they were.

00:35:58.285 --> 00:36:00.276
We'll remember.

00:36:00.320 --> 00:36:02.015
I know you will.

00:36:33.720 --> 00:36:36.655
I'd like to indulge in a new
custom that I've learned.

00:36:36.690 --> 00:36:38.123
It's called making a toast.

00:36:39.159 --> 00:36:42.128
To Captain Janeway
and her gracious crew.

00:36:42.162 --> 00:36:45.393
We are very grateful to you
for bringing us home.

00:36:45.432 --> 00:36:47.696
You will always
have friends here.

00:36:50.203 --> 00:36:51.727
Murderers.

00:36:51.771 --> 00:36:53.636
Lieutenant.

00:36:53.673 --> 00:36:56.506
You tried to hide
what you did, but I know.

00:36:56.543 --> 00:36:58.238
I saw everything.

00:36:58.278 --> 00:37:01.076
The Regressives, the executions.

00:37:01.114 --> 00:37:03.014
Wiping out an entire population,

00:37:03.049 --> 00:37:04.311
and then blaming them for it.

00:37:04.351 --> 00:37:06.410
This is most uncomfortable,
Captain.

00:37:06.453 --> 00:37:09.820
Perhaps a more private
discussion would be...

00:37:09.856 --> 00:37:11.084
No, that's what you've
been doing all along...

00:37:11.124 --> 00:37:12.091
hiding the truth.

00:37:12.125 --> 00:37:15.583
Hoping that it would
just die away quietly!

00:37:15.628 --> 00:37:17.858
Please.
This has to come out.

00:37:17.897 --> 00:37:19.057
I think it's time
we all understood

00:37:19.099 --> 00:37:20.896
what's been happening here.

00:37:20.934 --> 00:37:25.428
My dreams... they are real
memories from Jora Mirell.

00:37:25.472 --> 00:37:28.134
When she... when all
of them were younger,

00:37:28.174 --> 00:37:31.268
there was a group of people
they called Regressives.

00:37:31.311 --> 00:37:33.939
They just wanted to lead
a different kind of life,

00:37:34.013 --> 00:37:38.074
but... but they don't exist
anymore, do they?

00:37:38.118 --> 00:37:39.346
You exterminated them.

00:37:39.386 --> 00:37:42.412
These accusations
are completely untrue.

00:37:42.455 --> 00:37:45.049
You spent your whole life
covering it up,

00:37:45.091 --> 00:37:46.581
and then you realized

00:37:46.626 --> 00:37:49.220
that someone was passing
the memories on to me.

00:37:49.262 --> 00:37:50.889
So you...

00:37:50.930 --> 00:37:53.899
you used me to figure out
who it was

00:37:53.933 --> 00:37:55.264
and then you killed her,

00:37:55.301 --> 00:37:57.064
but, you know,
you were too late,

00:37:57.103 --> 00:38:00.436
because Korenna gave me the last
of her memories before she died.

00:38:00.473 --> 00:38:02.805
Korenna Mirell is dead?

00:38:02.842 --> 00:38:04.673
And you have evidence
that she was murdered?

00:38:04.711 --> 00:38:07.509
No, they made it look
like it was natural causes.

00:38:07.547 --> 00:38:09.014
You should know, Lieutenant,

00:38:09.048 --> 00:38:11.107
that I spoke
with Jora Mirell yesterday.

00:38:11.151 --> 00:38:12.140
I asked her specifically

00:38:12.185 --> 00:38:13.846
about the memories
you had experienced.

00:38:13.887 --> 00:38:15.479
She claimed not to know
anything about them.

00:38:15.522 --> 00:38:16.921
Of course she would say that.

00:38:17.023 --> 00:38:18.891
She was afraid for her life.

00:38:19.024 --> 00:38:19.888
No, you're lying.

00:38:19.925 --> 00:38:21.415
The Enarans would never
do anything

00:38:21.460 --> 00:38:22.552
like what you're saying.

00:38:22.594 --> 00:38:23.618
It's unthinkable.

00:38:23.662 --> 00:38:24.822
It is the truth.

00:38:24.863 --> 00:38:26.262
I know that you don't
want to believe it.

00:38:26.298 --> 00:38:27.925
In fact,
they're counting on that.

00:38:28.033 --> 00:38:29.466
They always have.

00:38:29.501 --> 00:38:31.162
I know B'Elanna and I trust her.

00:38:31.203 --> 00:38:33.501
It can't hurt to listen.

00:38:33.538 --> 00:38:35.631
Nobody thinks you're lying,
Lieutenant.

00:38:35.674 --> 00:38:39.075
The poor woman has been ill
for a long time.

00:38:39.111 --> 00:38:41.102
Her memories may be distorted

00:38:41.146 --> 00:38:44.309
or perhaps your perception
of them was colored

00:38:44.349 --> 00:38:46.112
by elements from your culture.

00:38:46.151 --> 00:38:47.379
No.

00:38:50.889 --> 00:38:53.790
I know that it's easier for you
to believe

00:38:53.825 --> 00:38:56.055
that I'm crazy or hallucinating,

00:38:56.094 --> 00:38:59.928
but this woman shared her life...
her whole identity... with me.

00:38:59.965 --> 00:39:02.058
I was with her
every step of the way

00:39:02.100 --> 00:39:04.500
as she convinced herself
that what she did...

00:39:04.536 --> 00:39:07.471
betraying the man she loved,

00:39:07.506 --> 00:39:10.236
playing her part
in the massacre...

00:39:10.275 --> 00:39:13.836
that it was all somehow
for the good of Enaran society.

00:39:13.879 --> 00:39:16.040
She showed me everything.

00:39:16.081 --> 00:39:20.040
No apologies, no request
for forgiveness,

00:39:20.085 --> 00:39:23.054
just the truth.

00:39:23.088 --> 00:39:26.216
At least she had the conscience

00:39:26.258 --> 00:39:31.355
to stand up and realize
what she'd done wrong...

00:39:31.396 --> 00:39:33.921
which is more
than I can say for you.

00:39:35.934 --> 00:39:37.424
I think it best that we...

00:39:37.469 --> 00:39:39.437
now prepare
for our departure, Captain.

00:39:39.471 --> 00:39:40.529
If you don't mind,

00:39:40.572 --> 00:39:43.632
I'd like to go to your Sick Bay
to attend Jora Mirell.

00:39:51.016 --> 00:39:52.711
I'm going to talk to the Doctor.

00:39:52.751 --> 00:39:55.481
I want to see you in my
ready room in one hour.

00:40:06.498 --> 00:40:08.830
I know that I could have found
a better way

00:40:08.867 --> 00:40:11.233
to handle the situation
than just charging

00:40:11.269 --> 00:40:12.566
into the mess hall like that.

00:40:12.604 --> 00:40:14.970
I was just too angry
to think straight.

00:40:15.040 --> 00:40:16.837
Not the first time that's
happened, I know,

00:40:16.875 --> 00:40:19.309
but if you had seen
what I saw...

00:40:19.344 --> 00:40:21.938
I might have done
exactly the same thing.

00:40:23.015 --> 00:40:24.414
You believe me.

00:40:24.449 --> 00:40:28.283
I believe that the memories
you experienced were real.

00:40:28.320 --> 00:40:29.947
Then we've got to do
something about it.

00:40:29.988 --> 00:40:32.149
We have to make this public.

00:40:32.190 --> 00:40:33.157
You tried that today.

00:40:33.191 --> 00:40:34.783
They didn't want to listen.

00:40:34.826 --> 00:40:37.124
Then we have to find proof.

00:40:37.162 --> 00:40:39.653
Let me go down to the planet.

00:40:39.698 --> 00:40:42.861
There must be some evidence left
of what really happened.

00:40:42.901 --> 00:40:44.835
Maybe there are
other people like Korenna

00:40:44.870 --> 00:40:46.633
who might be willing
to tell the truth.

00:40:46.671 --> 00:40:48.639
Whatever the Enarans have done,

00:40:48.673 --> 00:40:52.234
it's not our place
to bring them to justice.

00:40:52.277 --> 00:40:54.541
If they've chosen to conceal
part of their history

00:40:54.579 --> 00:40:56.638
from their own descendants,
that's their decision

00:40:56.681 --> 00:40:58.808
whether we approve of it or not.

00:40:58.850 --> 00:41:00.681
It's not just
a matter of history.

00:41:00.719 --> 00:41:01.811
This could happen again

00:41:01.853 --> 00:41:03.548
if no one knows
it happened before.

00:41:03.588 --> 00:41:06.216
We simply have no right
to get involved.

00:41:06.258 --> 00:41:09.421
Jora Mirell was murdered
on board this ship,

00:41:09.461 --> 00:41:11.429
which gives us a reason
to investigate.

00:41:11.463 --> 00:41:14.796
Maybe if we can expose
the reason why she was killed,

00:41:14.833 --> 00:41:16.926
the Enarans will start
to ask questions.

00:41:19.104 --> 00:41:21.902
I've gotten a full report
from the Doctor.

00:41:21.940 --> 00:41:23.931
He specifically looked
for evidence

00:41:23.975 --> 00:41:25.533
to support your accusations.

00:41:29.414 --> 00:41:30.847
He didn't find any.

00:41:30.882 --> 00:41:33.783
They could have used
their telepathy somehow,

00:41:33.819 --> 00:41:36.253
in some way that the Doctor
couldn't detect.

00:41:36.288 --> 00:41:39.257
We have no basis for
a murder investigation.

00:41:41.126 --> 00:41:44.027
I released her body
to the Enarans.

00:41:49.334 --> 00:41:51.598
So that's it?

00:41:51.636 --> 00:41:55.299
We just go on our merry way

00:41:55.340 --> 00:41:58.366
and nobody ever has to take
any kind of responsibility?

00:41:58.410 --> 00:42:00.537
I've canceled
our trade negotiations,

00:42:00.579 --> 00:42:02.012
as well as shore leave.

00:42:05.851 --> 00:42:08.911
We'll leave orbit as soon
as the Enarans are off the ship.

00:42:13.658 --> 00:42:14.750
B'Elanna?

00:42:14.793 --> 00:42:16.590
I believe the Enaran engineers

00:42:16.628 --> 00:42:19.927
are collecting the last
of their equipment right now.

00:42:21.566 --> 00:42:24.558
If there's anything more
you'd like to say to...

00:42:24.603 --> 00:42:26.264
any of them...

00:42:31.076 --> 00:42:33.271
Thank you.
Thank you, Captain.

00:42:42.220 --> 00:42:43.585
I'm relieving you.

00:42:46.158 --> 00:42:47.853
Can we talk for a minute?

00:42:47.893 --> 00:42:49.952
I have nothing to say to you.

00:42:49.995 --> 00:42:52.486
Then just listen.

00:42:52.531 --> 00:42:55.989
Like Harry said,
it couldn't hurt to do that.

00:42:56.067 --> 00:42:57.898
I'm leaving soon.

00:43:05.343 --> 00:43:07.140
I know you have
no reason to believe

00:43:07.179 --> 00:43:08.908
what I've said
about your people.

00:43:10.715 --> 00:43:12.546
All you have is my word

00:43:12.584 --> 00:43:15.417
against everything
you've ever been taught.

00:43:16.955 --> 00:43:18.047
That's right.

00:43:18.089 --> 00:43:20.387
So prove me wrong.

00:43:20.425 --> 00:43:25.226
Go down to Enara
and find the colony

00:43:25.263 --> 00:43:27.788
where the Regressives
were supposed to live.

00:43:27.832 --> 00:43:30.562
Talk to people.

00:43:30.602 --> 00:43:33.503
Ask questions.

00:43:33.538 --> 00:43:36.439
Learn the truth for yourself.

00:43:38.910 --> 00:43:41.970
Let me tell you
about my experiences.

00:43:42.013 --> 00:43:44.675
Maybe that will give
you someplace to start.

00:43:44.716 --> 00:43:47.412
I wish...

00:43:47.452 --> 00:43:48.942
I had your abilities.

00:43:48.987 --> 00:43:50.614
I could just show you.

00:43:51.823 --> 00:43:53.290
You would do that?

00:43:55.360 --> 00:43:57.487
Share your experiences openly?

00:43:57.529 --> 00:43:59.258
Of course.

00:43:59.297 --> 00:44:02.630
Then you'd know
I'm telling you the truth.

00:44:12.344 --> 00:44:15.404
I can make the connection
between us.

00:44:50.482 --> 00:44:52.279
What took you so long?
